Use Case 1: Help in the shower
Ablauf
- Upon command the help-i model will meet the user in preparation of a shower. 
- The robot will stand next to the user, on the side of the user's stronger (or still remaining) arm.
- The help-i model will be facing in the same direction as the user with its arm bent at 90 degrees angled in front of the user 
to allow the user to put as much body weight as they desire on the help-i model. 
- The model shall move simultaneously with the user to the shower until the shower's entry, at which time the help-i model will stand in the 
entrance to the shower with both arms ready to catch the user if they were to slip or need an arm to reat weight on. 
- If the user has a bath or a shower with a ledge that must be stepped over before showering, then before the user reaches the bath/shower the 
help-i model will bend down on one knee in front of the user at a 90 degree angle to the bath/shower and allow the user to have their 
weight on the help-i's hand, with help-i's other forearm being avaiable for the user to place their weight on it. 
- Once the user has finished showering the help-i model will either slowly lower the user out of the bathtub/shower, again allowing 
the user to simultaneously place their foot on one of help-i's hands, with the other hand being available to be used to support the user's arms 
or have both arms available to the user while it backs away from the user at the same pace the user is approaching it. 
- While the user could still slip the help-i model stands directly next to the user with a forearm held at a 90 degree angle ready for the user to 
place their weight on. 

Use Case 2: Microwave food preparation
- To initialise the help-i model connects with the smart microwave, setting the time for cooking and the temperature based on the 
instructions of the meal. 
- The help-i then picks up the meal and opens the microwave door through the connection and places the food inside.
- It stands and waits until the food has finised cooking, then opens the door, removes the food and places it on a bench.
- The help-i gets a suitable plate from the cupboard and scoops or pours the food out of the meal container onto the plate
or bowl. 
-The help-i model delivers the food to the user or on the user's behalf.

